      "writtenOn": "2023-08-25T03:44:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s unmodifiable by the caller, but since this object holds a ref to the underlying mutable collection, it can be mutated. Example\n\n    lp.addAssignedPrefix(prefix1);\n    final List\u003cIpPrefix\u003e assignedPrefixes \u003d lp.getAssignedPrefixes();\n    lp.addAssignedPrefix(prefix2);\n\nAfter this code, `assignedPrefixes` contains prefix2. This is likely unexpected, and you should probably make a defensive copy instead of an unmodifiable collection.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 929,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 929,
        "endChar": 30
      },
      "revId": "32a16a7e9fe0311b1696ce3d53e276fef896f487",
